{
  "_about": "MC-1558: every timing the hyper-v tests use, in one place. 'defaults' are generous, so a slow or loaded machine passes; a test that checks a timeout on purpose asks for 'narrow' values by name (scratch(name, { timing: 'narrow' }) for all of them, or { timing: ['HYPERV_MCP_READY_WAIT_MS'] } for some). To test a narrower result, tighten a value here. test/timing.test.js refuses literal waits in the test files.",
